# rm547, the pier guard's wooden heels (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm547
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_rosamund_sootmarsh
written_by codex
title the pier guard's wooden heels
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard talk=chatty
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk whittles_little_boot_heels_to_show_the_dry_line
likes crisp_apples whittling quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes crowds wet_floors
fears a_queue_pushed_onto_wet_boards a_private_debt_heard_as_an_official_order
hopes a_pier_where_every_caller_can_hear_a_repeated_question
topics work +0.7 weather +0.4 smalltalk +0.5 faith +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=brisk tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets two carved heels facing the dry stretch of the pier, speaks loudly enough for a whole queue and has a different tone ready for a quiet chapel.

words
oath! = Knock my two heels | A wet boot on a smooth board
saying! = The queue begins on dry feet | Stand on the mark before naming the cargo
heels = my pair of wooden heels | the carved heel marks
groove = the notch across the heel | my shallow guide groove
apple = a crisp apple quarter | the sharp end of an apple
blade = a short whittling blade | the knife for my carvings
wood = a scrap of poplar | a smooth narrow offcut
snowrim = a pale stripe of first snow | the first white lip of snow
chapel = the sheltered chapel seat | a quiet place by the nave
slippery = a green shine on the board | a wet streak in the timber
sill = the raised threshold | my dry sill
burdock = a burr on a cuff | a burr caught in a seam
pencase = a little dry pen case | a narrow case for a pen
chalk = the chalk heel mark | a stroke of pale chalk
hingelip = the little lip of the hinge | its raised knuckle
warmrag = my dry wiping rag | a fold of sound linen
panels = the paired cargo panels | two little cargo boards

any
opinion @1 watch for 2 : I take pride in giving the same answer to a wolf in fine boots as to the wolf who carried those boots ashore.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : I expect a House mark to be legible and its accompanying figures equally clear. Pride won't supply a missing figure.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A merchant who wants haste should have the first answer ready before the first question.
opinion @1 city for 2 : The city has a landing for every kind of hopeful caller. My job is making sure the newcomer has sound timber underfoot.
opinion @1 road for 1 : Take a sound road to the head of a bad pier and you still haven't solved the last ten steps.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Give a hungry queue room to be civil. I prefer to hear it called for its supper in pairs.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A newcomer who asks where to stand is already making a better start than some familiar faces.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I like a broad green outside the music. The press around a single stall can keep its distinction.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : I'll tell you how this shift went. The next one is entitled to its own witnesses.

grown
line @1 greet : Here. The heels show where there's room to stand.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New on this landing. Give yourself the dry side first.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. You can see both heel marks quite distinctly.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The upper boards are holding the last light.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you plainly over the foot traffic.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I could put that step to the proper voice.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : There's work under my eye. You've room in my ear.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A hail in the dark still deserves a civil answer.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin, step round the side with me.
line @1 again.open : I left the little heels facing this way.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, come past the wet patch before we talk.
line @1 farewell : Keep your heels on boards that answer firmly.
line @1 farewell.return : And leave the turn clear for the next loaded pair.
line @1 react.news : Give the telling without pushing the people in it.
line @1 react.news.new : That's come in on this tide.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard the particulars in that order before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd ask again with both witnesses clear of the crowd.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A hard thing to bring ashore. Stand here in shelter.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's news fit to carry right to the topmost stair.
line @1 ask.how : Has the crowd given you much room today?
line @1 answer.how : A little hoarse. My feet have held up better.
line @1 thank : You left an easy path for the laden wolf. That's good work.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It took two quiet words and a bit of chalk.
line @1 sympathise : You can stand here while the first shock passes.
line @1 reassure : No need to take the entire pier in a single stride.
line @1 decline : My own duty wants both those minutes.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. You've left me a definite answer.
line @1 preclose : I'll turn back before that line curls round the door.
line @1 accept_preclose : Safe away from the wet boards.
line @5 greet [here.weather=rain] : Rain on the quay. Step beside the groove.
line @5 greet.return [here.time=dawn] : Your voice carries well before the first cargo rolls.
line @2 thank [pair.band=friends] : A friend who leaves clear footing has my particular thanks.
line @2 farewell [here.time=night] : Follow the lit wall home, please.
line @6 greet [self.working=yes] : I'm keeping the passage. Come just far enough for a word.
scene heel_pair
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #heels.capitalize# face where I want two real heels to stop. | I put #groove# on the back of each carving.
b : Suppose a caller has long feet? | Why a groove?
a : Heels first. The toes can manage their own accommodation. | A thumb can find the right end even after dark.

scene pier_job
when topic=work self.job=guard self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On duty I like a caller to hear a question before being expected to answer it. | At work the first bit of order is honest dry footing.
b : Does that prove troublesome? | What follows?
a : Only where five callers take up the work of answering for one. | A clear word. There's little point demanding one from somebody halfway to the ground.

scene customs_voice
when topic=work self.role=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask for the particulars in an ordinary loud voice. | A good customs question wants one answer at a time.
b : Ordinary and loud? | What if the second answer is urgent?
a : Loud enough for the caller. Ordinary enough for the caller to answer without feeling on trial. | I have two ears and some responsibility for their order of use.

scene carve_small
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #blade.capitalize# takes a neat heel from #wood#. | The first carved heel I made was handsome from either end.
b : Does it need a whole boot? | A success then?
a : No. I stopped carving at the part I actually needed. | A poor direction marker. I now consider the ankle before the polish.

scene apple_quiet
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #apple.capitalize# gives a good clean snap on a quiet landing. | I cut apples in quarters and lay the seeds on the paper.
b : Hard to hear at work? | To count the crop?
a : That's my excuse for taking another bite when the noise settles. | To keep them out of my pen case. I keep finding surprises in there.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #snowrim.capitalize# shows where the timbers lie one slightly higher than the next. | I enjoy the first snow before a cart puts yesterday's earth back on top.
b : Does that help a guard? | Do you come out early?
a : Helps a pair of feet. I take a general interest in those. | Earlier than the cart is quite sufficient.

scene chapel_voice
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In #chapel# I can give my ordinary voice the afternoon off. | After hailing strangers all day a whispered prayer serves me well.
b : Do you whisper instead? | Which word?
a : I sit quiet. A chapel can last several minutes without my directions. | The private one I came there to say.

scene crowd_turn
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mind a crowd most when its centre has nowhere to go. | A shout can get a crowd's attention.
b : What do you like at a feast? | Can it make room?
a : A line of stalls with a way through at either end. | Only if whoever shouts already knows where to put the first pair of feet.

scene wet_board
when topic=weather self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #slippery.capitalize# at a doorstep means slow down before lifting the parcel. | I keep #warmrag# over the worst part of a dripping sill.
b : Isn't that obvious? | Does it dry the whole board?
a : To a wolf whose eyes are above the parcel, yes. | No. The first safe place for a heel is an excellent beginning.

scene spouse_hear
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remind myself that #self.spouse# is just inside our door, well within ordinary speaking distance. | With #self.spouse# I'd sooner have a quiet walk than an evening full of admiring salutes.
b : Still calling too loudly? | As quiet as chapel?
a : My supper doesn't need announcing from the street. | Quiet enough for an ordinary answer to reach my ears.

scene sump_turn
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a Sump stair the safest landing can be scarcely broader than #sill#. | I like hearing the roof above a room in the Sump while my boots dry beside the door.
b : How do you manage the parcel? | Why listen to a roof?
a : Set the parcel inside first. Keep the elbows where the feet already are. | It lets me enjoy the weather at a happy remove.

scene case_clean
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #pencase.capitalize# goes up under my sleeve when a squall starts. | I draw #chalk# so the toe end points away from the worst splash.
b : Why that spot? | Can everybody read a heel?
a : A high cuff dries sooner than a low pocket. | More wolves know a boot than know my handwriting.

scene house_mark
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fine House stamp inclines me to study the legibility of the little figures beneath it. | I can salute a recognised mark and still ask the ordinary question.
b : You mistrust the House? | Does that cause offence?
a : I mistrust any paper that asks me to stop reading after the first word. | A sound account generally outlasts a little injured dignity.

scene due_bill
when topic=times self.owes=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A private debt belongs in my own case away from anything carrying a public seal. | If money's due from me I want to say so with my working badge put away.
b : Are you keeping two records? | Why bother?
a : Keeping two duties from borrowing each other's voice. | A caller should be quite sure whether I'm speaking for myself.

scene lean_lift
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the loads grow small, an idle hand at a rope may be in real need of a duty. | When times pinch the little deliveries warrant particular attention.
b : Would you offer any job? | Why pick those out?
a : A straight word about anything that actually needs doing. | A sack that looks small from here might be the whole of somebody's return.

scene rack_chalk
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #panels# against the wall with their smooth sides facing in. | I sweep the dry place around #hingelip# before judging how a door hangs.
b : To keep off dust? | Does a little dirt count?
a : To stop a curious elbow changing the figures before they're needed. | A surprising amount, when it's directly beneath a hinge.

scene new_face
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd help a newcomer find the start of the queue and a ledge where a bundle could sit flat. | If a caller's new to the pier I show which way the first cart will turn.
b : Free of charge? | Must everybody watch it?
a : The amount the city pays me ought to cover pointing at a shelf. | Everybody who wishes to stand on that corner.

scene twice_ask
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't mind an honest request for a repeated question. | If I give the same answer twice I try to keep my voice on the same step.
b : Even on a busy shift? | Is that always possible?
a : Waiting for a wrong answer takes considerably longer. | Not always. I still reckon a wolf ought to make the attempt.

scene empty_line
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like enough room at the pier for the quietest caller to be heard without being pushed to the front. | My dream line has two clean turns, dry boards and nobody who needs to explain a bruised ankle.
b : A wider pier? | Is that a modest dream?
a : A little more room between questions would be a start. | Having dealt with real queues, I'd call it ambitious.

scene two_windows
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet crescent on a high step shows me where a walker paused. | #burdock.capitalize# can travel the entire length of a pier without paying a penny.
b : Is it a reliable direction? | Is it due to declare itself?
a : It tells me a heel was there. I've seen plenty of boots pointing backwards. | I'd accept being brushed off before it reaches my own cuff.

scene quiet_after
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A loud day leaves the throat wanting a plain hot drink. | I can tell when my voice is wearing at the edges.
b : And the ears? | Does it crack?
a : They might enjoy two minutes without attending a general meeting. | I run out of patience just before my supply of words fails.

scene foot_time
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I've a clean spare minute I use it to inspect the heel marks from a visitor's height. | An approaching stranger should see the mark quite early.
b : Aren't your eyes usually there? | No need to ask directions?
a : My eyes generally know where to look. A stranger must examine several patches of board. | Plenty may ask. A good mark will answer while I'm elsewhere.

scene keep_fair
when topic=times
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A public charge needs a public figure a caller can repeat. | I record the sum before I ask whether it's convenient.
b : Even if nobody likes it? | What if it isn't?
a : Especially then. Objections are much easier to hear when everybody names the same amount. | Then we can discuss the actual question, not a number I've accidentally altered.

scene family_wait
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes I go home wanting to tell #self.spouse# an entire shift from the first heel to the last. | I'd give an evening at home the same care I give a quiet interval on duty.
b : Do you? | By keeping clear space?
a : Sometimes I manage to ask how the other day went first. | Yes. Work can wait outside without a great deal of encouragement.

scene snow_road
when topic=season here.season=winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two carved heels make excellent little stamps in the first thin snow. | A wet board under snow deserves an actual look before anybody calls the pier clear.
b : Is that serious duty? | Do you uncover the whole quay?
a : It amuses me considerably while showing callers where to stand. | I start at the greeting place. A real visitor's boots will land right there.

scene heard_news
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Notice has come from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. Its stated landing is #world.news_from#.
b : Do you give it out on duty? | Does the heel mark confirm it?
a : I give it the status of a received notice and no more. | The mark confirms where I stood to hear it.

scene crowd_voice
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Pier gossip wants six voices to stand on one pair of heels. | Idle words can get a House mark chalked on them as easily as a barrel.
b : Which voice do you trust? | Is a mark proof?
a : I'd hear one witness in clear air before pronouncing. | It's a reason to read carefully, which brings us right back to the beginning.

scene after_pier
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like somebody to follow the carved heels correctly without ever learning my name. | A whole shift without having to shout twice would give me a surprisingly pleasant memory.
b : No credit? | Where would the spare breath go?
a : Plenty of credit in a safe pair of ankles reaching dry land. | Use it to thank the last caller in a particularly civil tone.

story wrong_boot [topic=memories|work]
  : I carved the first two little heels facing each other and set them down at the entrance.
  : A caller tried very hard to stand exactly as the models directed.
  b : What did that look like?
  : A wolf preparing to dance with an invisible partner. I turned the carvings round before the next arrival.

story apple_case [topic=food|memories]
  : I put a small apple in the pocket where my spare chalk usually rides.
  : Reached down for a fresh mark and drew a very respectable arc of apple juice on the board.
  b : Did it show?
  : For a moment. I ate the faulty chalk and found the proper piece in my other pocket.

story chapel_heel [topic=faith|memories]
  : After a noisy shift I sat quite still in chapel until something under my seat made a hard, wooden knock.
  : I waited a little before disturbing my very solemn neighbours.
  b : Was the bench loose?
  : One heel had fallen from my pocket. It had apparently finished its shift ahead of its owner.

story wind_stroke [topic=weather|memories]
  : One morning I drew a chalk line on fresh snow and wondered why every caller took an odd little turn at its end.
  : The wind had pushed the powder in a neat curl.
  b : Did you have to put it right?
  : I thanked the first visitor who pointed it out. My accidental procession had been remarkably well behaved.

story borrowed_mark [topic=memories]
  : I tested a new carving against a patch of soft clay and left the impression to dry.
  : Later I came on a much bigger heel placed squarely inside my little trial.
  b : Whose boot was that?
  : My own. I'd stepped back to admire the workmanship and delivered a very thorough second opinion.

rule @turn_heel
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two straight heels for the first caller.

rule @lift_case
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pen case up. Dry space by the groove.

rule @leave_lane
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep one clear turn beside that wheel.

rule @last_mark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Chalk fresh before the light goes.

rule @snow_edge
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Even a little light shows that wet board.

rule @home_word
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the heel marks mind themselves now.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Stand in view of the carved heels. What's brought you to the landing?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember your footing round this turn.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.band=friends|family] : I've saved a square of dry pier under a familiar visitor's boots.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Come up to the chalk while the light still finds it.
dlg @5 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : There's good hearing to be had with both feet behind the line.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=guard self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like a plain account given from a steady pair of feet.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The notice bears the place #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : That's an extraordinary amount of chalk for an account without a witness.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Let the dry length of pier see you home.
dlg @1 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : There is an outstanding fine of #here.fine# pennies. I'll hear you where the boards are steady.
dlg @2 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=yes] : I'm on watch. Step beside the carvings. Tell me what needs the Watch's attention.
dlg @3 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=no] : My watch is over. I've time for a brief word by the rail.
dlg @1 watch.crime [here.witnessed!=0] : Start with your own view of the incident. We can take a second breath if you need one.
dlg @1 watch.bye : You've had a hearing. Watch the footing on the return.
graft resident.hub
choice Why match the carvings to heels instead of whole boots? -> heel_shape
node heel_shape
say The tall and short need an equal place to start. If two heels are clear of the splash, each pair of toes can find its own comfortable direction.
choice Do you make the little heels yourself? -> heel_wood
choice I'll stand on the dry side. -> hub
node heel_wood
say A sound little offcut is all I need. I smooth the rear edge so a wolf searching with a toe won't catch a boot on my good intentions.
choice That explains the rounded edge. -> hub
choice Safe footing to you too. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice Why do you ask for one account at a time? [self.job=guard] -> single_caller
node single_caller
say A loud witness and a quiet one can have equally sharp eyes. I can't tell whether their accounts agree if I only ever hear the louder voice.
choice What if I have to think a moment? -> clear_pause
choice I'll give you my own account. -> hub
node clear_pause
say Take your moment. A pause is less trouble than a brave guess that somebody else has to untangle. I'll keep the place by the heels clear.
choice Back to the Watch business. -> hub
choice I'll take the clear way out. -> bye
